-- Definitions that nlg-owner-main.l4 imports. Each has a herald; the main module
-- reuses their names for definitions of its own, and a call must read the herald
-- of the definition it resolved to, not of one that has the same name.

-- A prefix function. The main module has a RECORD of the same name.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the distance from %x% to %y%
`Pt` x y MEANS y MINUS x

-- A mixfix function and a prefix function, on numbers. The main module defines
-- an operator with the same pattern and a prefix function with the same name on
-- strings, each with a herald of its own.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the smaller of %a% and %b%
`the lower of` a `and` b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the smaller number of %a% and %b%
`lower` a b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b
